WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.501
A dam collapses downriver

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.669
from the separation

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.204
nuclear plant, sparking fears

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:06.406
you can imagine about nuclear safety.

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:07.774
The UN's nuclear watchdog

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:09.476
says there's no immediate risk

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:11.611
and says they have enough water.

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:12.212
For months

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:13.013
you're sitting there in your mouth,

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:13.980
roughly the position of it.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:14.981
But the head of the International

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:16.549
Atomic Energy Agency

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:17.183
has been quoted

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:18.752
by Russian state media saying

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:19.753
they won't be able to keep

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:20.887
pumping cooling water

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:22.689
from a reservoir to the plant

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:25.025
if the water level drops too low.

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:26.192
Well, to explain all this,

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:28.161
the IAEA director General Rafael

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.295
Mariano Grossi,

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:31.264
joins me now live from Vienna.

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:31.865
Mr. Grossi.

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:33.400
Great to have you on the show.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.034
Thank you very much

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:36.069
for taking the time to speak to us.

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:36.803
Bring us up to date,

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:38.371
if you could, on the situation.

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:39.339
As you understand

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:40.173
right now

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:42.575
at the Zachary, your nuclear power plant.

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:43.810
Thank you.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:44.844
Thank you very much, as always, a

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:47.914
pleasure to talk to you.

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:48.648
What I can say,

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:50.717
we are monitoring this by the minute,

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:51.718
I should say,

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:54.220
since this occurred yesterday,

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:58.425
the levels of the of the water are,

00:00:58.425 --> 00:00:59.259
of course,

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:01.394
going down, decreasing quite,

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:03.496
quite rapidly.

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:05.632
Obviously, the dam down

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:08.435
south being destroyed

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:12.105
The effects of water is unimpeded.

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:13.706
And this is, of course,

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:15.909
having an automatic impact

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:17.343
on the amount of water

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:20.146
that the nuclear power plant has

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:24.551
to be integrated into the cooling system

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:25.819
of the plant.

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:27.854
I don't want to get too technical here,

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:29.823
but just to explain

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:32.725
that there is a reservoir there

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:36.896
and then a number of internal channels

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:38.765
that ensure that there is water

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:41.701
in circulation permanently, so to speak,

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:44.337
so that the reactors that you are,

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:47.140
you know, showing them there

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:50.743
to get the necessary cooling.

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:51.978
Of course,

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:56.182
if if the plant were to run out of water,

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:57.717
then we would have

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:59.486
a very serious situation.

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:02.655
What we said when I said is that there

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:05.625
doesn't seem to be an imminent

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:09.429
risk of a dry up of the water

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:12.198
available available there.

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:14.467
But the situation is serious

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.369
in Seoul insofar

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:19.239
as we are seeing this diminishing.

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:23.543
It's between five and seven centimeters

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:24.744
per hour.

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:28.548
So it's it's it's steady li going down.

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:30.216
So we have to monitor it

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:31.251
very, very carefully.

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:32.752
This is why I am going

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:35.121
back to the Parisian next week.

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:36.956
I've been there already.

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:39.526
Twice, and I'm going to return there

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:43.830
with a reinforced team of nuclear

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:47.066
safety experts from the from the IAEA

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:50.336
to two to have a more complete,

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:52.272
more comprehensive assessment

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:53.673
of where we are.

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:54.908
So no imminent risk.

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:56.876
But do you have a sense

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:57.844
of how much water

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:59.078
you would have into in some months,

00:02:59.078 --> 00:02:59.679
how many months

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:01.014
you have water in that

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:03.449
well before that cooling control?

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:05.552
I wouldn't like to speculate too much

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:07.921
because this is a function of the

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:11.357
the conditions of the water and how

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:14.060
we get to a point where the

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:17.096
the the the movement of the water.

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:19.499
The fact of water stabilized

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:20.934
is, relatively speaking.

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:23.403
I would say we calculate that

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:25.705
more or less a month is is guaranteed.

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:27.507
It could be a little bit more,

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:29.142
but it would also be less.

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:30.810
So it all depends.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:31.778
You were mentioning

00:03:31.778 --> 00:03:33.780
you were quoted as saying

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:36.349
that there is also a function

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:37.517
of the capacity

00:03:37.517 --> 00:03:40.186
to pump water from the river,

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:41.221
so to speak.

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:42.655
But there are certain levels

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:43.323
you can you must

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:44.490
you must imagine

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:45.758
that there is a difference

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:48.061
in the level of the of the reservoir

00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:49.262
and the

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:51.130
the cooling pond and the river itself.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:53.032
So you need to pump it up.

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:55.368
And then if the level goes down too much,

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:56.436
you cannot do that.

00:03:56.436 --> 00:03:58.371
So all of these things are

00:03:58.371 --> 00:03:59.105
in combination.

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:00.273
This is why we say

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:02.242
there is no reason for immediate panic

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:03.343
or to believe that

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:05.578
that the water to cool

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:07.914
the plant is going to dry up immediately.

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:09.816
But it's a serious situation.

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:11.784
We are taking this very seriously.

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:12.485
So no immediate.

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:14.821
But Ukraine says it will take a think.

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.122
They said five years Mr.

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:18.091
Grossi to rebuild the dam.

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:19.092
So I'm guessing you're

00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:21.327
looking now at plan B here.

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:23.463
Well, absolutely.

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:23.763
There are a

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:27.567
number of mitigation or mitigating.

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:30.303
If you want measures that can be taken,

00:04:31.404 --> 00:04:34.173
including using water from from

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:37.210
other places,

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:40.413
not necessarily the river

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:43.082
digging for for water in the water table

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:47.220
near the plant, getting water from

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:50.089
from neighboring towns or villages.

00:04:50.323 --> 00:04:52.558
But all of this needs to be assessed.

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:53.026
Of course,

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:56.362
the decision will be taken at the plant

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:59.799
But we as IAEA being present

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:01.334
there are going, of course,

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:03.036
to express very clearly

00:05:03.036 --> 00:05:05.505
what we feel should be should be done

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:09.542
Obviously, the situation and we we

00:05:09.676 --> 00:05:10.510
am aware

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:12.445
of of the assessment

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:14.447
by the Ukrainian government.

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:16.082
It is going to take a long time

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:18.318
to go back to those to the situation

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:20.586
before the accident.

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:24.524
But we were estimating this possibility.

00:05:24.524 --> 00:05:26.726
We were assessing this possibility

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:27.260
as one.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:29.162
We were wishing that it would not occur.

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:30.530
But unfortunately,

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:32.999
this has to be the case.

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:36.102
You call it an accident that Kiev accuses

00:05:36.269 --> 00:05:37.870
Russia of blowing up this dam,

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:40.173
sabotaging its own van dam.

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:42.375
What are your thoughts on this?

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:44.610
Well, there's there's no

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.579
if you sort of read too much into me

00:05:46.579 --> 00:05:47.980
using the word accident.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:48.715
It is, of course,

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:50.717
an event.

00:05:50.717 --> 00:05:52.251
It is a distraction.

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:54.921
I you know, I am the head of an agency

00:05:55.388 --> 00:05:56.522
that is an agency,

00:05:56.522 --> 00:05:57.657
among many other things

00:05:57.657 --> 00:05:59.826
we do of inspectors. We inspect.

00:06:00.393 --> 00:06:02.362
We are known as the nuclear watchdog,

00:06:02.362 --> 00:06:03.463
as you know.

00:06:03.463 --> 00:06:05.064
So we don't speculate

00:06:05.064 --> 00:06:07.834
when we pass judgment on something is

00:06:07.834 --> 00:06:09.869
on the basis of information

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:11.003
that we can assess.

00:06:11.003 --> 00:06:12.338
And as you can imagine,

00:06:12.338 --> 00:06:13.506
I don't have information

00:06:13.506 --> 00:06:14.640
to tell you

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:17.777
what we believe is at the origin of this.

00:06:17.777 --> 00:06:20.046
And there are a number of speculations

00:06:20.046 --> 00:06:23.149
that are out there on who is behind it.

00:06:23.249 --> 00:06:23.950
What I'm dealing

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:25.318
it is with their results,

00:06:25.318 --> 00:06:27.453
and I'm trying to prevent this

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:29.689
from getting into a nuclear accident.

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:32.759
Let's talk then about inside the plant,

00:06:32.759 --> 00:06:33.993
because as you would have seen Mr.

00:06:33.993 --> 00:06:35.228
Grossi from our correspondent

00:06:35.228 --> 00:06:36.362
and her son,

00:06:36.362 --> 00:06:37.363
Fred Pleitgen,

00:06:37.363 --> 00:06:38.731
you've seen hundreds of people

00:06:38.731 --> 00:06:40.166
being evacuated in the area.

00:06:40.166 --> 00:06:40.833
What has this

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:43.603
meant for the staff at the Zapper

00:06:43.603 --> 00:06:45.004
which power plant?

00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:45.772
Are there enough

00:06:45.772 --> 00:06:47.206
qualified people there

00:06:47.206 --> 00:06:49.509
to run the nuclear plant safely?

00:06:49.809 --> 00:06:52.111
Well, yeah, this is a good point.

00:06:52.545 --> 00:06:54.480
You know, this this this plant, it's

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:56.783
actually six reactors

00:06:56.783 --> 00:06:59.852
used to have around 12,000

00:07:00.386 --> 00:07:01.754
people working there.

00:07:01.754 --> 00:07:04.891
At the moment, we are below 3000.

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:09.529
And of course, one has to bear in mind

00:07:09.796 --> 00:07:11.531
that the plant at the moment

00:07:11.531 --> 00:07:13.633
is not operating normally.

00:07:13.633 --> 00:07:15.968
It's not generating power.

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:18.571
So it is at a very low level,

00:07:19.238 --> 00:07:20.706
at a low regime.

00:07:20.706 --> 00:07:23.976
So in this very low level operation,

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:27.914
we call it in the jargon, it shut down.

00:07:28.581 --> 00:07:29.649
You need far

00:07:29.649 --> 00:07:31.617
less people that you would need

00:07:31.617 --> 00:07:33.419
if the plant was operated,

00:07:33.419 --> 00:07:35.688
operating as in peacetime,

00:07:35.688 --> 00:07:37.190
which is not the case now.

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:39.525
But it's a matter that worries us.

00:07:39.525 --> 00:07:39.792
And I

00:07:39.792 --> 00:07:41.828
have been discussing this in Moscow

00:07:41.828 --> 00:07:44.897
and in Kiev, because quite clearly

00:07:45.231 --> 00:07:47.467
a situation like this is not sustainable

00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:48.634
for too long.

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:49.202
That will be

00:07:49.202 --> 00:07:50.403
there will be a moment

00:07:50.403 --> 00:07:52.772
where a decision will have to be taken

00:07:53.306 --> 00:07:53.806
as to

00:07:53.806 --> 00:07:55.041
whether the plant

00:07:55.041 --> 00:07:57.844
will be restarted or not.

00:07:58.110 --> 00:08:00.146
And then there might be a problem

00:08:00.146 --> 00:08:01.080
in terms of staff.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:03.583
This is only a quantitative analysis

00:08:03.583 --> 00:08:05.218
I am making. And I'm here.

00:08:05.218 --> 00:08:06.352
I'm conscious of the fact

00:08:06.352 --> 00:08:07.920
that I'm not talking about something

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.989
that worries me a lot also,

00:08:09.989 --> 00:08:11.991
which is that will affect the situation,

00:08:12.158 --> 00:08:12.992
the pressure.

00:08:12.992 --> 00:08:16.128
You have to remember that this plant

00:08:16.128 --> 00:08:17.597
is at the frontline,

00:08:17.597 --> 00:08:19.298
right at the frontline,

00:08:19.298 --> 00:08:20.600
not in the province,

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:22.902
not in the vicinity of the frontline.

00:08:23.102 --> 00:08:25.171
Whenever I go there, I have to,

00:08:25.171 --> 00:08:25.505
you know,

00:08:25.505 --> 00:08:27.373
go through the front line and through a

00:08:27.373 --> 00:08:28.708
no man's land.

00:08:28.708 --> 00:08:30.543
And with soldiers

00:08:30.543 --> 00:08:31.544
confronting each other,

00:08:31.544 --> 00:08:32.345
seeing each other,

00:08:32.345 --> 00:08:34.213
this is where the action is.

00:08:34.213 --> 00:08:36.883
So you can imagine working in both

00:08:37.083 --> 00:08:38.451
those conditions.

00:08:38.451 --> 00:08:39.685
And you were mentioning that

00:08:39.685 --> 00:08:42.121
a few days ago,

00:08:42.121 --> 00:08:44.257
some people were invited to evacuate

00:08:45.491 --> 00:08:47.126
a village near the plant.

00:08:47.126 --> 00:08:49.095
So the situation

00:08:49.095 --> 00:08:51.964
has nothing normal about it.

00:08:52.198 --> 00:08:54.667
It is very abnormal.

00:08:54.667 --> 00:08:56.969
And the levels of stress

00:08:57.136 --> 00:08:59.138
and anxiety are enormous.

00:08:59.138 --> 00:09:00.172
We are trying to help

00:09:00.172 --> 00:09:02.041
in that regard as well.

00:09:02.041 --> 00:09:03.342
I can't imagine the stress

00:09:03.342 --> 00:09:04.977
that they are all feeling across the.

00:09:04.977 --> 00:09:06.245
Appreciate you taking the time

00:09:06.245 --> 00:09:07.513
to speak to us this evening.

00:09:07.513 --> 00:09:08.047
Thank you, sir.

